{"archetypes":[{"name":"apply-path-divergence","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff refactors the old single Apply-all body into two named subsections: `### Apply-all body` (plan write only) and `### Shared post-apply pipeline` (dedup+EMIT_PLAN+validator+Step 2b.5). The auto-apply path chains Apply-all body → Shared post-apply pipeline; the manual one-by-one path skips Apply-all body and calls Shared post-apply pipeline directly after its own plan write. This asymmetric chaining is subtle and any divergence would silently break the invariant that both Gate B paths produce identical plan state.","prompt_body":"Examine `skills/design/references/approval-gates.md` closely, tracing how the auto-apply branch, the manual 'Apply all' option, and the one-by-one 'Go through each' option each reach `### Apply-all body` and `### Shared post-apply pipeline`. Verify that every path executes the dedup-sweep, `ACTION=EMIT_PLAN`, validator invocation, and Step 2b.5 exactly once and in the same order, with no step silently skipped on any branch. Check whether `approved-plan-findings.md` mutation (retain/append to rejected) happens before or after the `Shared post-apply pipeline` on the one-by-one path, and confirm that ordering matches the manual Apply-all path. Also check `scripts/test-design-structure.sh` to confirm its pins for `Execute \`### Apply-all body\` verbatim` count (≥2) and `Execute \`### Shared post-apply pipeline\` verbatim` count (=2) actually match the approval-gates.md content. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"gate-b-mode-resolution","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Gate B mode resolution has a 3-tier precedence chain (sourced MANUAL_REQUESTED session env → in-memory manual_requested → run-params.json) and the jq merge expression uses overwrite semantics for manual_gate_b (`= $merge_m`) vs OR semantics for partition/brainstorm. The 'true-only override' framing in approval-gates.md and the `test-design-structure.sh` pin for `manual_gate_b = $merge_m` must exactly match the SKILL.md code; any mismatch would cause the recovery path to silently auto-apply when --manual was passed.","prompt_body":"Read `skills/design/SKILL.md` Step 0b's Router-flag persistence block and `skills/design/references/approval-gates.md` §Gate B mode resolution. Verify that the jq `--argjson merge_m` expression and `.manual_gate_b = $merge_m` assignment in SKILL.md exactly matches the literal string pinned in `scripts/test-design-structure.sh`. Check whether the 'true-only override' semantics in approval-gates.md (session env and in-memory override take precedence as true-only; run-params.json is authoritative for false) are consistent with how SKILL.md writes `MANUAL_REQUESTED` to session env (only when `manual_requested=true`, omitting the flag when false) — specifically confirm this means a false in-memory value never overwrites a stale `MANUAL_REQUESTED=true` from session env. Examine whether Gate B's mode resolution correctly handles the case where the session env was written with `MANUAL_REQUESTED=true` in a prior run but run-params.json now says `false`. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"stale-prose-audit","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"This diff flips a fundamental behavioral default from 'user always prompted' to 'auto-apply'; the plan flags a specific failure mode where stale 'No-auto-apply' / 'user is always prompted' / 'explicit user choice' prose lingers in non-updated surfaces. SECURITY.md was updated but the diff does not show updates to `.github/workflows/`, `docs/topology.md`, `docs/run-logs.md`, agent prompt files, or other secondary references that might still assert the old no-auto-apply contract.","prompt_body":"Search across the repository (excluding the files modified in this diff) for prose containing 'explicit user choice', 'user is always prompted', 'never auto-applies', 'no auto-apply', 'user explicitly', or 'always prompts' in the context of Gate B or plan-finding application. Pay particular attention to agent prompt files under `agents/`, `.github/workflows/` CI steps, `docs/topology.md`, `docs/run-logs.md`, and any `.claude/rules/*.md` path-triggered rules that might reference Gate B semantics. Also check whether the `skills/design/scripts/plan-review-loop.sh` or sibling scripts contain any hard-coded comments or behavior that contradicts the new dual-mode contract. Report any stale occurrences that would mislead operators or downstream systems about whether Gate B prompts the user. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
